*> PLB-Q012 fetch-after-commit: a loop that fetches from a cursor and
*> commits, which closes a cursor not declared WITH HOLD.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. COMMITS.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-COUNT            PIC 9(5) VALUE 0.
01  WS-ID               PIC X(8).
01  WS-DONE             PIC X VALUE "N".
    EXEC SQL INCLUDE SQLCA END-EXEC.
    EXEC SQL DECLARE ACCT-CUR CURSOR FOR
        SELECT ACCT_ID FROM ACCOUNTS
    END-EXEC.
    EXEC SQL DECLARE HELD-CUR CURSOR WITH HOLD FOR
        SELECT ACCT_ID FROM ACCOUNTS
    END-EXEC.
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
MAIN-LINE.
    EXEC SQL OPEN ACCT-CUR END-EXEC
    *> Reported: every 100 rows, the commit closes ACCT-CUR.
    PERFORM UNTIL WS-DONE = "Y"
        EXEC SQL FETCH NEXT FROM ACCT-CUR INTO :WS-ID END-EXEC
        ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
        IF WS-COUNT = 100
            PERFORM COMMIT-WORK
        END-IF
    END-PERFORM
    *> Not reported: declared WITH HOLD.
    EXEC SQL OPEN HELD-CUR END-EXEC
    PERFORM UNTIL WS-DONE = "Y"
        EXEC SQL FETCH HELD-CUR INTO :WS-ID END-EXEC
        EXEC SQL COMMIT END-EXEC
    END-PERFORM
    *> Not reported: the loop opens the cursor again after it.
    PERFORM UNTIL WS-DONE = "Y"
        EXEC SQL OPEN ACCT-CUR END-EXEC
        EXEC SQL FETCH ACCT-CUR INTO :WS-ID END-EXEC
        EXEC SQL CLOSE ACCT-CUR END-EXEC
        EXEC SQL COMMIT END-EXEC
    END-PERFORM
    STOP RUN.
COMMIT-WORK.
    EXEC SQL COMMIT END-EXEC
    MOVE 0 TO WS-COUNT.
